        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          The word small hides a twenty-fold difference in performance. A mini thermoelectric dehumidifier and a compact 20-pint compressor unit can both be sold as small, but one is rated for about a pint of water a day under warm, wet test conditions and the other for twenty pints under cooler, harder ones. Pick the wrong type and you either own a night light that drips, or you put a full-size machine in a closet. This guide sorts them by the space you are trying to dry.
