            We wanted one honest answer for each kind of small space, so we picked across all three technologies rather than ranking six near-identical mini units. Two compact compressor dehumidifiers cover small rooms. Three thermoelectric units cover the range from a closet to a small bathroom or RV bedroom. One renewable desiccant box covers enclosed spaces with no outlet nearby.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Rated Removal and Test Conditions</h3>

          <p>
            For each unit we looked at the rated moisture removal and, critically, the test conditions behind it. Compressor units sold in the US are rated under the 2019 DOE procedure at 65 degrees Fahrenheit and 60% relative humidity, which is a realistic basement-ish condition. Mini thermoelectric units are usually rated at around 86 degrees and 80% humidity, which is a hot, humid summer day. Those two numbers are not comparable, and we say so wherever it matters.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Tanks, Power and Controls</h3>

          <p>
