        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Small dehumidifiers come in two sizes that have almost nothing in common. For a room people live in, buy a 20 to 22 pint compressor unit: the Midea Cube 20 if footprint matters, the Midea MAD22C1AWS if efficiency and price matter more. For a closet, cabinet, safe or RV locker, buy a mini: the EDV-2400 if you want a humidistat, the EDV-1100 or PB-03 for a simple plug-in, the E-333 where there is no outlet.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Convert ounces to pints before you compare, close the door to the space you are drying, and put a hygrometer in the room. If the reading never drops below 50%, the unit is too small, whatever the box says.
          </p>
